            <ArticleTitle>A dramatic synergistic effect of a flexible achiral linker on a rigid chiral cis-1,2-diamine bifunctional organocatalyst.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2892-2896</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6ob02743a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The combination of a &quot;rigid&quot; chiral bicyclic cis-1,2-diamine skeleton with steric bulkiness and a &quot;flexible&quot; achiral linker was newly designed as a bifunctional organocatalyst framework and it showed excellent catalytic activity of up to 0.05 mol%, accompanied by the reversal of enantioselection depending on the position of the linker, in an amine-thiourea organocatalyzed asymmetric Michael reaction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
